Compare local paths case-sensitively off Windows.

IsPathToSameFile tells whether two local paths name the same file with
SameText, ignoring case, as Windows' file systems do. POSIX file systems
are case-sensitive: there "/home/u/WinSCP.ini" and "/home/u/winscp.ini"
are two files, which it took for one (TConfiguration::MoveStorage then
skipped the move; TGUIConfiguration took a PuTTY path for the default one). They are compared with SameStr when the
platform's delimiter is not a backslash: on Windows SameText as before, so
upstream's behaviour is unchanged. Line counts are unchanged.

Offered upstream as winscp/winscp#88, with an #ifdef _WIN32 as the
maintainer prefers: the same choice made at compile time, carried here as
one line to keep the line count; dropped when a pin move brings it in.

--- a/source/core/Common.cpp
+++ b/source/core/Common.cpp
@@ -957,1 +957,1 @@
-  bool Result = SameText(CanonicalPath1, CanonicalPath2);
+  bool Result = (PathDelim == L'\\') ? SameText(CanonicalPath1, CanonicalPath2) : SameStr(CanonicalPath1, CanonicalPath2);
